    "youtubeId": "Fj2sXv0u-0g",
    "keyNotes": "• What is Food and Nutrition?\n  - Food: Any nourishing substance eaten or drunk to sustain life, provide energy, promote bodily growth, and protect against diseases.\n  - Nutrients: Chemical components found in food that the human body absorbs and utilizes.\n• The Six Classes of Nutrients:\n  1. Carbohydrates: Primary source of bodily energy. Found in cassava, yam, plantain, maize, millet, rice, bread.\n  2. Proteins: Essential for growth, tissue repair, and enzyme production. Composed of amino acids.\n     * Animal Sources (First Class / Complete Protein): Fish, eggs, chicken, beef, milk.\n     * Plant Sources (Second Class / Incomplete Protein): Beans, cowpeas, groundnuts, soya beans, bambara groundnuts.\n  3. Fats and Oils (Lipids): Concentrated energy store, body insulation, and carrier for fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K). Found in palm oil, shea butter, coconut oil, groundnut oil, butter.\n  4. Vitamins: Organic protective substances required in micro-quantities:\n     * Vitamin A: Healthy eyesight and skin (carrots, red palm oil, dark leafy greens). Deficiency: Night blindness.\n     * Vitamin B Complex: Cellular energy release, nerve function (cereals, eggs, liver). Deficiency: Beriberi, pellagra.\n     * Vitamin C (Ascorbic acid): Wound healing, immunity, gum health (oranges, lemons, guavas, tomatoes). Deficiency: Scurvy.\n     * Vitamin D: Calcium absorption and strong bone formation (sunlight synthesis, fish liver oil, eggs). Deficiency: Rickets.\n  5. Mineral Salts: Inorganic elements:\n     * Iron: Hemoglobin synthesis in red blood cells (kontomire/cocoyam leaves, liver, meat). Deficiency: Anemia.\n     * Calcium & Phosphorus: Strong bones and teeth (milk, small bones of fish like keta school boys / salmon).\n     * Iodine: Thyroid gland hormone regulation (iodated salt, seafood). Deficiency: Goitre.\n  6. Water and Dietary Fiber (Roughage):\n     * Water: Solvent, digestion, waste excretion, body temperature control.\n     * Roughage / Fiber: Indigestible cellulose that stimulates intestinal peristalsis, preventing constipation.\n• Indigenous Ghanaian Food Commodities Classification:\n  - Roots and Tubers: Cassava, yam, cocoyam, sweet potato.\n  - Cereals and Grains: Maize, rice, millet, sorghum.\n  - Legumes and Oilseeds: Cowpeas, bambara beans, groundnuts, agushie (melon seeds).\n  - Animal Foods: Tilapia, mudfish, tuna, beef, mutton, bushmeat.\n  - Fruits and Vegetables: Kontomire, garden eggs, okro, tomatoes, mangoes, pawpaw.",
